---
// The front page: what barbican does, next to its UI, then what it covers, how the pieces fit, how to install it, what
// changed recently, and where to read on.
import { Code, Tabs, TabItem } from '@astrojs/starlight/components';
import Changelog from './Changelog.astro';
import Screenshot from './Screenshot.astro';
import { releases } from '../changelog';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
const link = (path: string) => `${base}${path}`;
const download = 'https://github.com/nikarh/barbican/releases/latest/download';

const covers = [
	[
		'Log sources',
		'A container’s log through the Docker API, a file followed across rotation, the systemd journal, or a VictoriaLogs query. Parsers for Traefik, OpenSSH and Authelia, or a regular expression.',
		'/guides/sources/',
	],
	[
		'Rules',
		'Match paths, methods, statuses, hosts, user agents, user names and blocklists; ban once a threshold is reached in a window. Defaults cover exploit probes, scanners and password guessing.',
		'/guides/rules/',
	],
	[
		'Trust and ban lengths',
		'Addresses people log in from are trusted. Lengths per rule, country, network and blocklist, longer for repeat offenders.',
		'/guides/rules/#the-policy',
	],
	[
		'nftables over netlink',
		'One table of its own. Bans are set elements with timeouts, written over netlink one small change at a time; the kernel lifts them on time even with the agent stopped.',
		'/internals/firewall/',
	],
	[
		'Countries and feeds',
		'Block countries and continents, and lists such as Spamhaus DROP. Allow lists too, such as Cloudflare’s ranges for sites behind its proxy.',
		'/guides/feeds/',
	],
	[
		'A web UI',
		'What every address tried and what was decided, live; rules, lengths, countries and lists are edited there. Works on a phone, and behind your proxy’s authentication.',
		'/guides/ui/',
	],
	[
		'Edge agents',
		'A small agent for OpenWrt, or iptables and ipset on other firmware, blocks what the agents ban for the whole network. Bans are pushed to it over a binary protocol.',
		'/edge/overview/',
	],
	[
		'History',
		'Import months of old logs through the rules, as though they had been read live, straight from VictoriaLogs if that is where they are.',
		'/guides/import/',
	],
	[
		'Small',
		'One process and a SQLite database: about 70 MB with 25 000 bans and three continents blocked. The edge agent is a megabyte, and uses 6 to 10 MB.',
		'/reference/resources/',
	],
];
---

<div class="home not-content">
	<section class="intro">
		<div class="lead">
			<p class="summary">
				Bans addresses that abuse your services. barbican reads the logs of a reverse proxy, an SSH server and an
				authentication portal, decides with rules what counts as abuse, and blocks offenders with nftables.
			</p>
			<p>
				It blocks on the server and, through a small edge agent, on routers for the whole network. Countries and public
				blocklists can be blocked as a whole. A web UI shows what every address tried and what was decided, and is where
				the rules are edited. It is what fail2ban, a log pipeline and a dashboard do together, in one process.
			</p>
			<div class="actions">
				<a class="button primary" href={link('/start/quick-start/')}>Quick start</a>
				<a class="button" href={link('/start/introduction/')}>Read the docs</a>
				<a class="button" href="https://github.com/nikarh/barbican">Source on GitHub</a>
			</div>
			<p class="meta">Linux with nftables; OpenWrt and iptables routers. MIT or Apache-2.0. Written in Rust.</p>
		</div>
		<div class="shot">
			<Screenshot
				name="overview"
				alt="barbican's overview: bans and events of the last 30 days, recent bans, the firewall, feeds, sources and edges, bans by country and events by rule."
			/>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="covers">
		<h2>What it does</h2>
		<dl>
			{
				covers.map(([term, text, href]) => (
					<div>
						<dt>
							<a href={link(href!)}>{term}</a>
						</dt>
						<dd>{text}</dd>
					</div>
				))
			}
		</dl>
	</section>

	<section class="flow">
		<h2>How the pieces fit</h2>
		<div class="flow-grid">
			<pre
				class="diagram"
				role="img"
				aria-label="Logs go through a parser and the rules into the engine, which records to SQLite and blocks with nftables on the host; an edge API pushes the blocks to edge agents, which block with nftables on routers.">{` logs ─► parser ─► rules ─► engine ─► SQLite
 (docker, file,     │          │
  journald,     (in each   bans, trust
  VictoriaLogs)  source)       │
                               ▼
                    nftables (this host) ── edge API ──► barbican-edge ─► nftables (router)`}</pre>
			<p>
				The <strong>agent</strong> runs on each server whose logs it reads and blocks there. <strong>Edge agents</strong> on
				routers follow one or more agents and block the union of what they ban, so an address banned for probing one
				server can’t reach any of them. See <a href={link('/internals/how-it-works/')}>How it works</a>.
			</p>
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="phone">
		<div class="phone-text">
			<h2>On a phone</h2>
			<p>
				The UI is one page and one WebSocket, served by the agent or by a small container next to your other services.
				It works under a path prefix and behind forward authentication, and its layout follows the screen: on a phone the
				panels stack, the grids keep the columns that matter, and the tabs move to the bottom.
			</p>
			<p><a href={link('/guides/reverse-proxy/')}>Behind a reverse proxy</a> · <a href={link('/guides/ui/')}>The web UI</a></p>
		</div>
		<div class="phones">
			<Screenshot name="overview-phone" alt="The overview on a phone." />
			<Screenshot name="bans-phone" alt="The bans on a phone." />
		</div>
	</section>

	<section class="install">
		<h2>Install</h2>
		<p>
			Static binaries and packages for x86_64 and aarch64, edge agents for OpenWrt and for routers without nftables.
			Release files are signed. Details are in <a href={link('/install/overview/')}>Install</a>.
		</p>
		<Tabs syncKey="distro">
			<TabItem label="Debian / Ubuntu">
				<Code
					lang="bash"
					code={`arch=$(dpkg --print-architecture)    # amd64 or arm64
curl -fLO "${download}/barbican_\${arch}.deb"
sudo apt install "./barbican_\${arch}.deb"`}
				/>
			</TabItem>
			<TabItem label="Arch Linux">
				<Code
					lang="bash"
					code={`curl -fLO "${download}/barbican-$(uname -m).pkg.tar.zst"
sudo pacman -U "barbican-$(uname -m).pkg.tar.zst"`}
				/>
			</TabItem>
			<TabItem label="OpenWrt">
				<Code
					lang="bash"
					code={`cd /tmp    # the edge agent and its LuCI pages; armv7, aarch64 or x86_64
wget ${download}/barbican-edge-armv7.apk
wget ${download}/luci-app-barbican.apk
apk add --allow-untrusted ./barbican-edge-armv7.apk ./luci-app-barbican.apk`}
				/>
			</TabItem>
		</Tabs>
		<p class="after">
			Then say where the logs are, and start it in dry run first: <code>[firewall] enabled = false</code> decides and
			records everything, and blocks nothing.
		</p>
	</section>

	{
		releases.length > 0 && (
			<section class="changes">
				<div class="changes-head">
					<h2>Recent releases</h2>
					<a href={link('/reference/changelog/')}>All releases</a>
				</div>
				<Changelog limit={3} level={3} skip={['Documentation']} />
			</section>
		)
	}

	<section class="next">
		<h2>Reading order</h2>
		<ol>
			<li><a href={link('/start/introduction/')}>Introduction</a>: the parts, and what barbican isn’t.</li>
			<li><a href={link('/start/quick-start/')}>Quick start</a>: one server, one log, a dry run, then blocking.</li>
			<li><a href={link('/guides/sources/')}>Sources</a> and <a href={link('/guides/rules/')}>rules</a>: what is read, and what counts as abuse.</li>
			<li><a href={link('/edge/overview/')}>Edge agents</a>: blocking for the whole network on a router.</li>
			<li><a href={link('/reference/configuration/')}>Configuration</a>: every setting.</li>
		</ol>
	</section>
</div>

<style>
	.home {
		--gap: clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: calc(var(--gap) * 1.25);
		margin-top: 0.5rem;
	}
	.home > *,
	.intro > * {
		min-width: 0;
	}
	.home h2 {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xl);
		font-weight: 650;
		letter-spacing: -0.01em;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
	}
	.home a {
		color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
		text-underline-offset: 0.2em;
		text-decoration-thickness: 1px;
	}

	.intro {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 0.8fr) minmax(0, 1.2fr);
		gap: var(--gap);
		align-items: start;
	}
	.lead p {
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
		line-height: 1.65;
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		max-width: 38rem;
	}
	.lead .summary {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-xl);
		line-height: 1.5;
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
		text-wrap: pretty;
	}
	.actions {
		display: flex;
		flex-wrap: wrap;
		gap: 0.6rem;
		margin: 1.5rem 0 1.25rem;
	}
	.button {
		display: inline-flex;
		align-items: center;
		padding: 0.5rem 0.95rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-gray-5);
		border-radius: 6px;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		font-weight: 600;
		color: var(--sl-color-white) !important;
		text-decoration: none;
		transition: border-color 160ms cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1), background-color 160ms cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
	}
	.button:hover {
		border-color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
		background: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
	}
	.button.primary {
		background: var(--sl-color-accent);
		border-color: var(--sl-color-accent);
		color: var(--sl-color-black) !important;
	}
	.button.primary:hover {
		background: var(--sl-color-accent-high);
		border-color: var(--sl-color-accent-high);
	}
	.lead .meta {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-3);
	}
	.shot :global(.screenshot) {
		margin: 0;
	}

	.covers dl {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr));
		gap: 0 1.5rem;
		margin: 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline-light);
	}
	.covers dl > div {
		padding: 1rem 0 1.1rem;
		border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
	}
	.covers dt {
		font-weight: 650;
		margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
	}
	.covers dt a {
		color: var(--sl-color-white);
		text-decoration: none;
	}
	.covers dt a:hover {
		color: var(--sl-color-text-accent);
		text-decoration: underline;
	}
	.covers dd {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
		line-height: 1.55;
	}

	.flow-grid {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
	}
	.diagram {
		margin: 0;
		padding: 1rem 1.25rem;
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline-light);
		border-radius: 6px;
		background: var(--sl-color-gray-6);
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-1);
		font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.8rem;
		line-height: 1.5;
		overflow-x: auto;
	}
	.flow p,
	.phone p,
	.install p,
	.next li {
		color: var(--sl-color-gray-2);
	}
	.flow p {
		margin: 0;
		max-width: 50rem;
	}

	.phone {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) auto;
		gap: var(--gap);
		align-items: start;
		/* The heading's rule, across both columns. */
		border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
		padding-top: 1.25rem;
	}
	.phone h2 {
		border-top: none;
		padding-top: 0;
	}
	.phone-text p {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
		max-width: 34rem;
	}
	.phones {
		display: flex;
		gap: 1rem;
	}
	.phones :global(.screenshot) {
		margin: 0;
		width: 15rem;
	}

	.install p {
		margin: 0 0 1rem;
	}
	.install .after {
		margin-top: 1rem;
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
	}
	.install code {
		font-family: var(--__sl-font-mono);
		font-size: 0.86em;
		color: var(--bc-code-text);
		background: var(--sl-color-bg-inline-code);
		border: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
		border-radius: 4px;
		padding: 0.08em 0.32em;
	}

	.changes-head {
		display: flex;
		align-items: baseline;
		justify-content: space-between;
		gap: 1rem;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--sl-color-hairline);
		padding-top: 1.25rem;
		margin-bottom: 1rem;
	}
	.changes-head h2 {
		margin: 0;
	}
	.changes-head a {
		font-size: var(--sl-text-sm);
	}

	.next ol {
		margin: 0;
		padding-left: 1.25rem;
		display: grid;
		gap: 0.35rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 64rem) {
		.intro {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
		.covers dl {
			grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
		}
		.phone {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
	}
	@media (max-width: 40rem) {
		.covers dl {
			grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr);
		}
		.lead .summary {
			font-size: var(--sl-text-lg);
		}
		.phones :global(.screenshot) {
			width: auto;
			flex: 1 1 0;
			min-width: 0;
		}
	}
</style>
